                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course is a mandatory professional course for students in the five-year program in stomatology, covering the following four modules:</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;"><strong>Child Patient Reception and Behavior Management</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 1: Introduction</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 2: History Taking, Oral Examination, and Treatment Planning for Pediatric Oral Diseases</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 6: Behavior Management for Children in Pediatric Dental Visits</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;"><strong>Oral Development and Developmental Abnormalities in Children</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 3: Anatomical Morphology and Tissue Structure Characteristics of Primary Teeth and Young Permanent Teeth</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 4: Growth and Development of the Maxillofacial Region and Dentition in Children</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 5: Dental Developmental Abnormalities</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 11: Occlusal Guidance</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;"><strong>Main Diseases Threatening Children's Oral Health</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 7: Dental Caries in Children</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 8: Pediatric Pulp and Periapical Diseases</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 9: Dental Trauma in Children</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 10: Periodontal Diseases and Oral Mucosal Diseases in Children</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 12: Pediatric Oral Surgery</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;"><strong>Impact of Systemic Diseases on Children's Oral Health</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 13: Dental Treatment for Children with Disabilities</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">· Chapter 14: Oral Manifestations of Systemic Diseases in Children</p>
<p style="line-height: 1;">&nbsp;</p>
<p>Please refer to the teaching content arrangement for specific chapters.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
